        },
        "texto": "Though concealed from sight in the upper chamber, the lamentations of the bereaved king could be easily heard by his followers, for he “cried with a loud voice.” These loud exclamations are alluded to in several other places. At Jacob’s funeral there was “a great and very sore la…"
      },
      "c-b3c6d36c1eda0c59": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-286",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "This is the only passage where a ferry-boat is named, and some critics think that a mere crossing of a ford is meant. The Hebrews could not have been ignorant of the use of boats, since they were employed by the Egyptians, as is evident from the monuments. The king’s servants may…"
      }
